== Walkthrough ==

"Skeletal miners" are at the zoneline of Paineel in southern Toxxulia. Observe their back-and-forth dialogues:

:[[abandoned heretic pet]] says 'Blast you skeletons!  Why I ever ressurected you, I don't know!!'
:abandoned heretic pet says 'Speed up the digging my pets!!'
:[[a skeleton (miner)]] says 'We are not your pets!!'
:a skeleton says 'We will speed up when you return our mining caps. There are falling rocks all over this place!! We could get killed!!'

[[Useless Cloth Cap]] can sometimes be looted from [[a kobold scout (Toxxulia)|a kobold scout]]. Take a Cap to the two skeleton miners (or the abandoned heretic pet) at the entrance to [[Paineel]].

;Talrigar Eklorin
[[Talrigar_Eklorin|Talrigar]] wanders the Paineel side of the river in Toxxulia.  When he is near [[a skeleton (miner)]] you may sometimes observe the following dialogue:
: Talrigar Eklorin says 'How many times must I remind you,.. YOU ARE ALREADY DEAD!! I shall find a young apprentice to [seek out the mining caps].'
When hailed the following dialogue becomes available
You say, 'Hail, Talrigar Eklorin'
:Talrigar Eklorin says, 'This is no place for adventures of any sort. You had best leave before your bones join in on my private task. Heed my words, unless of course you are a [practitioner of the black arts]'
You say, 'I am a practitioner of the black arts'
:Talrigar Eklorin says, 'So you are a fellow necromancer? You have chosen the most powerful circle of magic. You are wise. I seek to employ a young necromancer to [seek out two mining caps]'
You say, 'I will seek out two mining caps'
:Talrigar Eklorin says, 'Somewhere within this forest are two Mining Caps. They are nothing more than cloth caps which I used to fake my summoned pet's working within the cave nearby. They were stolen by a couple of kobold scouts. Return these caps to me and I shall reward thee. Maybe even with knowledge of Necromancy.'
Upon turning in '''TWO''' [[Useless Cloth Cap]]:
:Talrigar Eklorin says, 'Good work. I can now silence the continual whining of my skeletons. Here young apprentice, your reward. Ask for nothing more.'

{{exp}}

